    rdfs:label "Evidence for Almonds used in Perfumery, Pomades & Essential Oils: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. PERFUMERY, ART OF"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "orange flower, 2d operation. 4 drachms of essence of bitter almonds. 4 drachms of balsam of Peru. 4 ounces of essence of lemons. Eau de Cologne. Two processes have been adopted for the preparation of this perfume, distillation and infusion; the first of which, though generally abandoned, is, however, the preferable one."@en ;
